#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551286 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32904df2-4f2b-512e-b905-4f4eebcb813e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550488} {:answer/id #uuid "b50b8760-3a6d-55c4-a188-c37cf457dc61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550863} {:answer/id #uuid "e8fc2b8c-e26a-5dd7-a42a-b9a4b347b89f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 12 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550998} {:answer/id #uuid "f98c45d9-1ef2-58e4-b974-3eb63756e062" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -12 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551036} {:answer/id #uuid "ffcf0b97-a0e4-515d-9606-6b57bb04f711" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551057}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186550863} :answer-field/id #uuid "f732bcd0-c8c8-5638-93ed-8a183c2c0d4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551224}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6ad7a8de-9677-5fd6-a871-171f20886f2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130788" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the elementary matrix \n$$\n\\displaystyle N=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{12}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $N$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply an elementary row operation that transforms the left matrix into the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}[N\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{12} & 0 & 1\\end{array}] &  & {R}_{2}:=12{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{array}{cc|cc}1 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 12\\end{array}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse is obtained on the right-hand side of our big matrix after the transformation. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{N}^{-1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}]}
